## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of non-blocking data structures, ABA avoidance, memory ordering, and NUMA-aware performance under mixed-priority traffic. It also touches on backpressure and practical microbenchmark design.

## Key Concepts
- Lock-free design and ABA avoidance with per-slot sequence counters
- Memory ordering: release on enqueue, acquire on dequeue
- NUMA-aware layout and cache-line alignment
- Priority routing, backpressure metrics, and spillover handling
- Correct wrap-around handling and bounded capacity

## Code Example
```javascript
// Ring buffer with 64-bit sequence per slot
struct Slot {
    alignas(64) uint8_t data[64];
    std::atomic<uint64_t> seq;
};

class Ring {
    Slot buffer[N];
    std::atomic<uint64_t> head{0}, tail{0};

public:
    bool enqueue(const void* payload) {
        uint64_t pos = tail.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
        uint64_t seq = buffer[pos & mask].seq.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
        if (seq != pos) return false; // full or wrap-around
        memcpy(buffer[pos & mask].data, payload, 64);
        buffer[pos & mask].seq.store(pos + 1, std::memory_order_release);
        return true;
    }

    bool dequeue(void* payload) {
        uint64_t pos = head.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
        uint64_t seq = buffer[pos & mask].seq.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
        if (seq != pos + 1) return false; // empty
        memcpy(payload, buffer[pos & mask].data, 64);
        buffer[pos & mask].seq.store(pos + N + 1, std::memory_order_release);
        head.store(pos + 1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
        return true;
    }
};

// Two rings per priority, producer selects based on flag
```

## Performance Measurement
- **Latency**: Use RDTSC/RDTSCP around enqueue/dequeue, measure percentiles under mixed priority ratios (90/10, 50/50)
- **Backpressure**: Count enqueue failures per ring, track queue depth, measure producer stall time
- **NUMA**: Pin threads to sockets, allocate buffers locally, measure remote memory penalties
- **Throughput**: Vary producer/consumer ratios, monitor cache miss rates with perf

